    title: "Russia agrees to ban recruitment of Ghanaian nationals for Ukraine war",
    summary: "Russia has agreed to stop the recruitment of Ghanaian nationals to fight the war in Ukraine, Accra said in a statement.",
    preview: "Ghana Russia has agreed to stop the recruitment of Ghanaian nationals to fight the war in Ukraine, Accra said in a statement. President Putin reportedly gave the assurance on the sidelines of last week’s Russia-Africa summit in Moscow after his Ghanaian counterpart, John Mahama, raised the issue. Ghana last month said its citizens were being \"tricked\" into joining the Russian war effort and urged Moscow to do more to halt the practice.",
    body: "Ghana\n\nRussia has agreed to stop the recruitment of Ghanaian nationals to fight the war in Ukraine, Accra said in a statement.\n\nPresident Putin reportedly gave the assurance on the sidelines of last week’s Russia-Africa summit in Moscow after his Ghanaian counterpart, John Mahama, raised the issue.\n\nGhana last month said its citizens were being \"tricked\" into joining the Russian war effort and urged Moscow to do more to halt the practice.\n\nAs of mid-August, more than 270 Ghanaians had fought for Russia and at least 62 have been killed in the fighting; an additional 15 are missing.\n\nNow President Putin has said he will ban Ghanaians from participating, whether through irregular recruitment or voluntary enlistment.\n\nSeveral African countries including Kenya, South Africa, Nigeria, Cameroon and The Gambia have complained that their citizens have been lured to fight under false promises of work or educational opportunities.\n\nUkrainian officials last week reported that a Botswanan citizen recruited through social media was killed in Ukraine’s Luhansk region.",
